IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja1-part3-div2-procedure.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- LAYER 1, Part 3, Division 2 "Original jurisdiction" (continued): ss 17B (oral hearing not needed), 17C (summary dismissal of an appeal from the Registrar) and 18 (powers of the General Division).
-- The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text. Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` only.
-- The twin provisions are encoded on their own (ruling E1, option C): s 22A (appellate civil matters) is in scja1-part3-div4-6; ss 37, 38, 55, 56 belong to scja2.

§ `Part 3: General Division of High Court (continued)`

§§ `Division 2: Original jurisdiction (continued)`

§§§ `Section 17B: Oral hearing not needed generally`

-- s 17B(1). Plain gloss: may the General Division decide this matter, in its original civil jurisdiction, without hearing oral arguments? Not a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules
-- ("other than": read as the text's no, question QE; fork F6).
-- src:1236 | 17B.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), the General Division may
-- src:1237 | decide any matter in its original civil jurisdiction without hearing oral
-- src:1238 | arguments, other than a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court or the
-- src:1239 | Family Justice Rules.
@ref s 17B(1) (src:1236-1239)
GIVEN `the matter is in the original civil jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter within the General Division's original civil jurisdiction?
      `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules prescribe as needing oral arguments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17B(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the matter is in the original civil jurisdiction of the General Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matter in its original civil jurisdiction"
        IF `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 17B(2). (1) does not allow any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given (including any part of a trial of an action) to be conducted without an oral hearing, unless all the parties consent.
-- src:1241 | (2) Subsection (1) does not allow any part of a proceeding where
-- src:1242 | oral evidence is given (including any part of a trial of an action) to be
-- src:1243 | conducted without an oral hearing, unless all the parties consent.
@ref s 17B(2) (src:1241-1243)
GIVEN hearing IS A Hearing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17B(2) section 17B(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT hearing's `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given"
        IF hearing's `all the parties consent` THEN JUST TRUE -- the "unless" is met ("unless all the parties consent"), so (2) no longer denies what (1) allows; this function asks what (1) allows, not whether the court may grant (fork F16)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not allow any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given ... to be conducted without an oral hearing, unless all the parties consent"

-- s 17B(3). In any matter that the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments, it may direct that the matter be heard asynchronously by exchange of written correspondence, subject to (4).
-- src:1245 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), the General Division may, in any
-- src:1246 | matter that the General Division may decide without hearing oral
-- src:1247 | arguments, direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner
-- src:1248 | by exchange of written correspondence with the party or parties using
-- src:1249 | such means of communication as directed by the General Division.
@ref s 17B(3) (src:1245-1249)
GIVEN `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17B(3) the General Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any matter that the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments"

-- s 17B(4). The General Division must not hear a matter asynchronously if that would be inconsistent with its duty to ensure the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties.
-- src:1251 | (4) The General Division must not hear a matter in an asynchronous
-- src:1252 | manner if to do so would be inconsistent with the court’s duty to
-- src:1253 | ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties.
@ref s 17B(4) (src:1251-1253)
GIVEN `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would hearing the matter in an asynchronous manner be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17B(4) the General Division must not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty"

-- s 17B(4) as a regulative rule (ruling N2: derived from the decision above). The bearer is "the General Division"; no time is stated.
DECLARE `s 17B(4) party` IS ONE OF `s 17B(4) the General Division`
DECLARE `s 17B(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 17B(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner`
    `s 17B(4) takes some other step in the matter`

@ref s 17B(4) must not hear a matter in an asynchronous manner (src:1251-1253)
GIVEN `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 17B(4) party` `s 17B(4) act`
`s 17B(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` MEANS
    IF `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties`
    THEN PARTY `s 17B(4) the General Division`
         SHANT `s 17B(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner`
         WITHIN 1
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 17B(4): the General Division heard the matter in an asynchronous manner when to do so was inconsistent with its duty to ensure fairness to all parties"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 17B(5). To avoid doubt, s 17B does not affect the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding a matter that may be decided without them.
-- src:1255 | (5) To avoid doubt, this section does not affect the power of the
-- src:1256 | General Division to hear oral arguments before deciding any matter
-- src:1257 | that may be decided without hearing oral arguments.
@ref s 17B(5) (src:1255-1257)
GIVEN `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17B(5) section 17B affects the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section does not affect the power of the General Division to hear oral arguments"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matter that may be decided without hearing oral arguments"

§§§ `Section 17C: Summary dismissal of certain matters`

-- s 17C(1). Plain gloss: may a Judge sitting in the General Division, on his or her own motion, summarily dismiss this appeal against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings? Only if the Judge is
-- satisfied of (a) or (b). The Judge's satisfaction is the court's judgment, asked as a fact. Limb (a) is the ground shared with ss 22B(1)(b), 38(1)(b) and 56(1)(b) (PLAN.md difficulty 7); its input is this section's own.
-- src:1263 | 17C.—(1) A Judge sitting in the General Division may, on his or
-- src:1264 | her own motion, summarily dismiss any appeal made against a
-- src:1265 | decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings, if the Judge is
-- src:1266 | satisfied of any of the following:
-- src:1268 | (a) every issue in the appeal has already been decided by the
-- src:1269 | General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of
-- src:1270 | Appeal in an earlier matter in which the appellant was
-- src:1271 | involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit;
-- src:1273 | (b) such conditions as may be prescribed by the Rules of Court
-- src:1274 | or the Family Justice Rules are met.
@ref s 17C(1) (src:1263-1274)
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal made against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings?
      `s 17C(1)(a) every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge satisfied that every issue in the appeal has already been decided by the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and that the appeal therefore has no merit?
      `s 17C(1)(b) the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge satisfied that the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17C(1) a Judge sitting in the General Division may on his or her own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal is against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any appeal made against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings"
        IF `s 17C(1)(a) every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 17C(1)(b) the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are met` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Judge is satisfied of any of the following"

-- s 17C(2). Before summarily dismissing an appeal, the Judge must (a) give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause and (b) consider the appellant's representations.
-- A bare "must" not done answers NOTHING for the dismissal: the text states a duty and does not say what follows (question QB; fork F7).
-- src:1276 | (2) Before summarily dismissing any appeal under subsection (1), a
-- src:1277 | Judge sitting in the General Division must —
-- src:1284 | (a) give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause
-- src:1285 | why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed; and
-- src:1287 | (b) consider any representations of the appellant.
@ref s 17C(2) (src:1276-1287)
GIVEN `the appellant was given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why your appeal should not be summarily dismissed?
      `the Judge considered the representations of the appellant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Judge consider your representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17C(2) the Judge may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 17C(1) now, as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appellant was given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed` AND `the Judge considered the representations of the appellant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Before summarily dismissing any appeal under subsection (1), a Judge sitting in the General Division must (a) ... and (b) ..." states a duty and does not say what follows if it is not done (fork F7)

-- s 17C(2) as a regulative rule (ruling N2: derived from the decision above). The bearer is "a Judge sitting in the General Division"; no time is stated.
DECLARE `s 17C(2) party` IS ONE OF `s 17C(2) the Judge sitting in the General Division`
DECLARE `s 17C(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 17C(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause`
    `s 17C(2) considers the representations of the appellant`

@ref s 17C(2)(a) give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause (src:1276-1285)
GIVEN `the Judge is about to summarily dismiss the appeal under section 17C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 17C(2) party` `s 17C(2) act`
`s 17C(2) the Judge must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` MEANS
    IF `the Judge is about to summarily dismiss the appeal under section 17C(1)`
    THEN PARTY `s 17C(2) the Judge sitting in the General Division`
         MUST `s 17C(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause`
         HENCE PARTY `s 17C(2) the Judge sitting in the General Division`
               MUST `s 17C(2) considers the representations of the appellant`
               HENCE FULFILLED
               LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 17C(2)(b): the Judge must consider the representations of the appellant"
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 17C(2)(a): the Judge must give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 17C(3). In s 17C, "appeal" includes part of an appeal.
-- src:1289 | (3) In this section, “appeal” includes part of an appeal.
@ref s 17C(3) (src:1289)
GIVEN `it is an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an appeal?
      `it is part of an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it part of an appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17C(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 17C` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is part of an appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section, “appeal” includes part of an appeal"

§§§ `Section 18: Powers of General Division`

-- s 18(1). The General Division has the powers vested in it by any written law for the time being in force in Singapore.
-- src:1295 | 18.—(1) The General Division has the powers that are vested in it
-- src:1296 | by any written law for the time being in force in Singapore.
@ref s 18(1) (src:1295-1296)
GIVEN `a written law in force in Singapore vests the power in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law in force in Singapore vest the power in the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the General Division has the power vested in it by a written law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a written law in force in Singapore vests the power in the General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the powers that are vested in it by any written law for the time being in force in Singapore"

-- s 18(2). Without limiting (1), the General Division has the powers set out in the First Schedule. Seam 1 of PLAN.md: the First Schedule (scja3) answers whether the power is one it sets out.
-- A power the Schedule does not set out is not thereby denied ("without limiting"): NOTHING.
-- src:1300 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the General Division has the
-- src:1301 | powers set out in the First Schedule.
@ref s 18(2) (src:1300-1301)
GIVEN `sch 1 the power is one set out in the First Schedule` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the General Division has the power set out in the First Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1 the power is one set out in the First Schedule`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting subsection (1)": a power outside the First Schedule may still be vested by a written law
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the First Schedule's answer is not given

-- s 18(3). The powers in (2) are exercised in accordance with any written law, Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules relating to them.
-- src:1305 | (3) The powers mentioned in subsection (2) are to be exercised in
-- src:1306 | accordance with any written law, Rules of Court or Family Justice
-- src:1307 | Rules relating to them.
@ref s 18(3) (src:1305-1307)
GIVEN `sch 1 the power is one set out in the First Schedule` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(3) the power is to be exercised in accordance with the written law, Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules relating to it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1 the power is one set out in the First Schedule`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The powers mentioned in subsection (2)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the First Schedule's answer is not given
